  "description": "A Field Maple tree (T1) approximately 9m in height, situated on the right-hand side boundary of the rear garden at Herne Hill United Reformed Church, adjacent to the fence with the car park off Red Post Hill.  \r-Crown to be thinned by 30% including the removal of dead wood; \r-Crown to be reduced by 2.5m whilst retaining the basic shape of the tree; \r-Branches to be pruned at convenient growth points.\r\rThe tree currently overshadows PV panels on the roof of the church, reducing energy generated by approximately 15%. The reduction and removal of dead wood will preserve the tree whilst promoting the generation of renewable energy, helping Southwark to meet its climate emergency targets.",
